# Voyagely – Architecture & Folder Structure

## Folder Structure – Feature-Based

Organize code by **feature domain**, not by file type. Each feature is self-contained with its own components, hooks, services, and types.

```
src/
├── features/                    # Feature modules (core product domains)
│   ├── trips/
│   │   ├── components/          # Trip-specific components
│   │   │   ├── TripCard.tsx
│   │   │   ├── TripSettings.tsx
│   │   │   └── ConstraintForm.tsx
│   │   ├── hooks/               # Trip-specific hooks
│   │   │   ├── useTrip.ts
│   │   │   └── useTripMembers.ts
│   │   ├── services/            # Trip API / business logic
│   │   │   └── tripService.ts
│   │   ├── types.ts             # Trip-specific types
│   │   └── index.ts             # Public API of this feature
│   ├── activities/
│   │   ├── components/
│   │   ├── hooks/
│   │   ├── services/
│   │   ├── types.ts
│   │   └── index.ts
│   ├── voting/
│   ├── scenarios/
│   ├── chat/
│   └── auth/
│
├── components/                  # SHARED / reusable UI primitives
│   ├── Button.tsx
│   ├── Modal.tsx
│   ├── Toast.tsx
│   ├── Card.tsx
│   ├── Skeleton.tsx
│   ├── ErrorMessage.tsx
│   └── Layout.tsx
│
├── hooks/                       # SHARED hooks (cross-feature)
│   ├── useAuth.ts
│   ├── useLanguage.ts
│   └── useTheme.ts
│
├── lib/                         # Core infrastructure
│   ├── supabase.ts              # Supabase client instance
│   ├── realtime-service.ts      # Realtime subscription manager
│   ├── store.ts                 # Zustand global store (keep thin)
│   ├── errorHandling.ts         # Central error utilities
│   ├── i18n.ts                  # i18next config
│   ├── sentry.ts                # Sentry config
│   ├── analytics.ts             # PostHog config
│   ├── utils.ts                 # Pure utility functions
│   ├── types/                   # Shared / database types
│   │   └── database.types.ts
│   └── locales/                 # Translation JSON files
│       ├── en.json
│       ├── fr.json
│       └── ...
│
├── pages/                       # Route-level page components
│   ├── LandingPage.tsx          # Assembles features for landing
│   ├── LoginPage.tsx
│   ├── SignupPage.tsx
│   ├── DashboardPage.tsx
│   └── TripDetailPage.tsx
│
├── App.tsx                      # Router + providers
└── main.tsx                     # Entry point
```

## Dependency Direction (Critical Rule)

Dependencies must flow **downward** only. Never import upward or sideways between features.

```
pages → features → components / hooks / lib
                 ↘ lib (services, types, utils)

components (shared) → lib only (never import from features)
hooks (shared) → lib only (never import from features)
lib → nothing above it
```

**Concrete rules:**

- A **page** can import from any feature, shared component, hook, or lib.
- A **feature** can import from shared components, shared hooks, and lib. Never from other features directly.
- A **shared component** can import from lib only. Never from a feature.
- **lib** modules must not import from features, pages, or shared components.

If two features need to share data, use:

- A **shared hook** in `src/hooks/`.
- The **Zustand store** in `src/lib/store.ts`.
- A **React Context** at a higher level (App or page).

## Feature Module API (index.ts)

Each feature folder has an `index.ts` that exports its public API. Other code imports from the feature via this file, not from internal paths.

```typescript
// features/voting/index.ts
export { VotingPanel } from './components/VotingPanel';
export { useVotes } from './hooks/useVotes';
export type { Vote, VoteResult } from './types';

// In a page:
import { VotingPanel, useVotes } from '@/features/voting';
// NOT: import { VotingPanel } from '@/features/voting/components/VotingPanel';
```

## When to Create a New Feature Module

Create a new `features/xxx/` folder when:

- The domain has its own **data model** (table in Supabase).
- It has **3+ components** specific to that domain.
- It has its own **hooks or services**.

Don't create feature folders for trivial utilities or single-component concerns — those go in `components/` or `lib/`.

## Migration Path

The current codebase may not match this structure yet. When touching a file:

- If it belongs to a feature, move it to the correct feature folder.
- Don't refactor the entire codebase at once — migrate progressively, feature by feature.

